+# T-0161 — Billing source edited after its draft: amend or flag the draft, and a Sync issues view for billing issues
+
+## Goal
+After T-0069 drafts the invoice for a Closed Won Opportunity / activated Order, later changes of the source (lines added, prices changed, Opportunity reopened) only bump salesforce_billing_trigger.later_events (DL-0373, RQ-0124 F5). Decide and build what a later change does to a still-draft invoice (rebuild the draft lines, or raise a billing issue for a person), and show app.salesforce_billing_issue rows in the Sync issues inbox.
+
+## Context (design refs)
+- Created 2026-11-09 by claude as a follow-up of [T-0069](T-0069.md) (RQ-0124, DL-0370..DL-0375).
+- Specs: [UC-01](../../Docs/specs/UC-01.md)
+
+## Scope
+- Research the rule (draft only; approved/posted invoices are never touched — credit note path).
+- Inbox: billing issues (PERIOD_LOCKED, LINES_INCOMPLETE, UNKNOWN_ACCOUNT, …) next to the inbound issues, with ignore/retry.
+
+## Open questions (→ research before start)
+- [ ] Amend vs flag is a product choice inside UC-01 A-flows; research first, log the decision.
+
+## Acceptance criteria (each maps to a test + SS id; add an SS row at claim)
+- [ ] AC-1 (db-integration) A line added to a drafted Opportunity changes the draft (or raises an issue) per the decided rule; a posted invoice is never changed.
+- [ ] AC-2 (e2e-playwright) Billing issues appear in the Sync issues inbox with code, source and message (screenshot).
+
+## Steps
+- [ ] 1. Resolve open questions → `Docs/research/RQ-NNNN-*.md` and link in `research:`
