+# T-0163 — Write back the invoice status for every sales-invoice transition (manual approve, post, from the AR module)
+
+## Goal
+T-0069 writes one invoice.drafted / invoice.posted write-back event for invoices it creates (DL-0373). Invoices approved or posted later by a person (approveSalesInvoice / postSalesInvoice) write nothing back yet, so Opportunity.LF_Invoice_Status__c stays "Draft". Emit the T-0067 contract v1 snapshot from the AR lifecycle for every transition of an invoice that has a Salesforce source.
+
+## Context (design refs)
+- Created 2026-11-09 by claude as a follow-up of [T-0069](T-0069.md) (RQ-0124, DL-0370..DL-0375).
+- Specs: [UC-01](../../Docs/specs/UC-01.md)
+
+## Scope
+- A write-back hook in packages/modules/ar (like the notifier) fed with the Salesforce link from salesforce_billing_trigger.
+- One event per transaction with the final status (DL-0373); amount invoiced on the Opportunity.
+
+## Open questions (→ research before start)
+- [ ] none
+
+## Acceptance criteria (each maps to a test + SS id; add an SS row at claim)
+- [ ] AC-1 (db-integration) Manual approval then posting of a Closed Won draft writes one invoice.posted event; the Opportunity reads Posted with the amount invoiced.
+- [ ] AC-2 (db-integration) An invoice without a Salesforce source writes no write-back event.
+
+## Steps
+- [ ] 1. Resolve open questions → `Docs/research/RQ-NNNN-*.md` and link in `research:`
